OL,3,ALego marketplace BrickLink offline
OL,4,Aafter 'unusual activity' detected
OL,5,
OL,6,FLego has taken its online marketplace
OL,7,FBrickLink offline after detecting what
OL,8,Fit described as unusual activity on the
OL,9,Fplatform.
OL,11,FBrickLink is used by Lego collectors
OL,12,Fworldwide to buy and sell second-hand
OL,13,Fsets, source new bricks and purchase
OL,14,Flimited edition releases.
OL,16,FIt was originally set up by a fan but
OL,17,Facquired by Lego in 2019. The firm
OL,18,Fwrote on its homepage that before
OL,19,Frestoring BrickLink, it wanted to
OL,20,F"fully understand" what had happened.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,115,105,200,160,0,100
